<exercise xml:id="q-green-centroid">
<title>The centroid of a lamina</title>
<statement>
<p>
A lamina of constant density <m>\delta</m> occupies a region <m>R</m> in
the <m>xy</m>-plane with boundary <m>C</m>, oriented counterclockwise.
Show that its centroid (<xref ref="def-centroid"/>) has the coordinates
<md>
<mrow>
\bar{x} \amp = \frac{1}{2A} \oint_C x^2\, dy
\quad \text{and}
</mrow>
<mrow>
\bar{y} \amp = -\frac{1}{2A} \oint_C y^2\, dx,
</mrow>
</md>
where <m>A</m> is the area of the region bounded by <m>C</m>.
</p>

<sidebyside width="97%">
<image>
<latex-image>
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[rounded corners=8pt, draw=gray!55, thick] (0,0) rectangle (15,18);
\node[anchor=north west, text=gray!60, font=\footnotesize\itshape]
  at (0.25,17.75) {workspace};
\end{tikzpicture}
</latex-image>
<shortdescription>Blank workspace for showing the two line-integral formulas for the centroid.</shortdescription>
</image>
</sidebyside>
</statement>
</exercise>

